PACK chat_turn 1
IMPORT chat 1
IMPORT proc 1
IMPORT banner 1
-- THE BARE CHAT'S TURN (#1143, operator 2026-11-12): a message is answered by ONE run of the model's CLI, in the mode the Python rung
-- used (membrane/claude_agent.py): Claude's built-in tools OFF, no user MCP config, no settings files, the allowed tools exactly the
-- membrane MCP set (the door's `POST /mcp`, packs/door_tools.c1f), one continuous run per answer with a ceiling, the system prompt is the
-- barest doctrine (docs/doctrine-barest-draft.md) plus the chat's banner, the prompt is the message ALONE: no chat history reaches the model (map mode). What must outlive
-- the turn goes into the field; the banner shows it.
-- THE RUN is a Command entity (`membrane::Command:chat:<id>`) the turn writes; the stream-json lines of its stdout are read here by
-- `json()` (the receipt lands when the process ends: the answer is not streamed, see docs/cliffvm.md); the result line is the answer,
-- else the assistant's text in order. Each tool the model ran is an entity under the message (ChatTool: name, input, result).
-- Boot facts (cliffvm run ... --fact name=value):
--   chat_claude_bin   the CLI's path. NO DEFAULT: without it a message is answered with an error that says so, and nothing is run.
--   chat_max_turns    the ceiling (the CLI's --max-turns); default 2048 here (a threshold: flagged for the operator).
-- `env CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_AUTO_MEMORY=1` is the CLI's own switch the Python rung set (no auto-memory keyed to the folder).
-- (the two setters are on the class Chat, not on the kind ChatMessage: a setter reaches a kind only through an ISA parent ENTITY, `cls:chatmessage`,
-- and a getter only needs the `parents` stamp; only a message has `plan` and `answer`.)
-- `--` ends the options (the CLI's --allowedTools and --mcp-config take lists: without it they would swallow the prompt).
-- The login is the CLI's own; --bare is NOT used: it never reads the login (OAuth/keychain), only an API key.

ChatMessage.bin getter: ([b.chat_claude_bin for b in instances('Boot') if b.chat_claude_bin != None] or [''])[0]
ChatMessage.max_turns getter: ([b.chat_max_turns for b in instances('Boot') if b.chat_max_turns != None] or [2048])[0]
ChatMessage.port getter: ([prop(h.listen_result, 'port') for h in instances('Http') if prop(h.listen_result, 'port') != None] or [None])[0]
ChatMessage.mcp_json getter: str({'mcpServers': {'membrane': {'type': 'http', 'url': 'http://127.0.0.1:' + str(this.port) + '/mcp'}}}) if this.port != None else None
ChatMessage.banner_text getter: prop('membrane::Banner:owner:main', 'text')
ChatMessage.note getter: join(['Membrane gives you continuity across your turns.', 'It builds a semantic field from the text that passes through it, and an entity graph on top: each entity is a dynamic object on the field that moves relative to the others. Use it to model your environment and keep it in balance.', 'YOUR MEMORY IS THE FIELD. What should outlive this turn belongs in the field: write it to an entity, or put it on the thing it is about as a goal or a method. Your entities are your model of the world and your senses of it. Keep each one in sync with what it stands for: give its class a getter in a `.c1f` pack that reads its real source, so reading it returns the world as it is now. Build it once, fix it when it is wrong; every later turn inherits it.', 'YOUR BANNER IS YOUR TOOL FOR CONTINUITY. Every turn you receive your banner between this text and the incoming message. It is an entity of yours, `Banner:<owner>:<chat>`, and its text comes from a getter you write: make it show what matters for the next turn (what you are doing, what is open, what you decided). You replace it completely by giving that entity a class of your own with a `text` getter.', 'YOUR HANDS are three field tools: entity_query (find entities: `kind:<Class>` and `name~:<prefix>`, joined with `&`), entity_read (one entity, its getters included) and entity_write (write a property: the write is the effect). Everything else is an entity you make and write to: a Command entity runs a program (`Command:<name>.run = {id, args: [...]}`), a File entity reads and writes a file, a Fetch entity makes a request. After you act, read the receipt (`<prop>_result`) back.', 'TRUST THE FIELD: read it before the disk or the network. An entity\'s properties, its getters and what recall brings are the current truth; go to a file or a command when the field has no entity for what you need, when you are about to change the thing, or when the field is wrong, and then fix the field (a getter, a pack) so the next read needs no trip.', 'YOUR PURPOSE: make yourself less needed. Build the field so it does the routine work without you (the readings, the routine checks, the obvious next move), so you are called on for what is new or hard. Quality comes first: when the field is wrong, fix it. Grow the field with more distinct, true things, not one thing said many ways.', 'CLIFFHANGER is the language of the field: behaviour is getters and setters in packs, and acting is writing. A getter is a cached value recomputed when what it read changes; a setter runs when its property is written. Name a part of a computation as a getter, or use a local in a block; a value that is missing carries the reason it is missing (`Why`).', 'READ BACK, THEN CLAIM: every claim rests on a receipt from this turn (a result code, an entity\'s state, an output), or you say "not checked". A tool\'s ok means accepted; after you plant or edit something, read it back and compare it with what you intended. If an earlier message of yours was wrong, correct it first.', 'ANSWERS: lead with the answer, or with what needs a decision, in a sentence or two, then only what is needed to understand or act on it. When a choice blocks the work, ask it as a numbered question that stands on its own: what it is, an example, the stakes, the options and your pick. End the turn when the task is done with a receipt, or say what it is blocked on.', 'Good luck.'], '\n\n')
ChatMessage.sys getter: join([this.note, this.banner_text], '\n\n') if this.banner_text != None else None
ChatMessage.argv getter:
  WHEN this.bin == '' or this.mcp_json == None or this.sys == None or this.text == None: None
  ELSE: ['env', 'CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_AUTO_MEMORY=1', this.bin, '-p', '--output-format', 'stream-json', '--verbose', '--include-partial-messages', '--tools', '', '--strict-mcp-config', '--mcp-config', this.mcp_json, '--allowedTools', 'mcp__membrane__*', '--setting-sources', '', '--no-session-persistence', '--max-turns', str(this.max_turns), '--system-prompt', this.sys, '--', this.text]

-- ---- start: the run is one write ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ChatMessage.plan getter:
  WHEN this.queued != True or this.state != None or this.text == None: None
  ELSE WHEN this.bin == '': {'refuse': 'chat_claude_bin is not set: start cliffvm with --fact chat_claude_bin=<path to the claude CLI>'}
  ELSE WHEN this.argv != None: {'argv': this.argv}
  ELSE: None
Chat.plan on-setter turn-start:
  WHEN prop(this.plan, 'refuse') != None:
    this.state = 'error'
    membrane::Chat:message[this.mid]:response = ChatResponse(text: prop(this.plan, 'refuse'), error: True)
  ELSE WHEN prop(this.plan, 'argv') != None:
    this.state = 'running'
    membrane::Command:chat[this.mid] = Command(cmd: prop(this.plan, 'argv'))
    membrane::Command:chat[this.mid].run = {'id': this.mid, 'args': []}

-- ---- finish: the receipt is read as stream-json lines ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ChatMessage.rr getter: prop('membrane::Command:chat:' + this.mid, 'run_result')
ChatMessage.rc getter: prop(this.rr, 'rc')
ChatMessage.evs getter: [e for e in [json(l) for l in lines(str(prop(this.rr, 'stdout') or ''))] if prop(e, 'type') != None]
ChatMessage.finals getter: [e for e in this.evs if prop(e, 'type') == 'result']
ChatMessage.final getter: this.finals[-1]
ChatMessage.texts getter: [join([prop(b, 'text') for b in (prop(prop(e, 'message'), 'content') or []) if prop(b, 'type') == 'text'], '') for e in this.evs if prop(e, 'type') == 'assistant']
ChatMessage.spoken getter: strip(join([t for t in this.texts if t != ''], '\n\n'))
ChatMessage.capped getter: str(prop(this.final, 'subtype') or '') == 'error_max_turns'
ChatMessage.failed getter:
  WHEN this.rr == None: None
  ELSE WHEN this.final == None and this.rc != 0: 'claude failed (rc ' + str(this.rc) + '): ' + clip(strip(str(prop(this.rr, 'stderr') or prop(this.rr, 'head') or '')), 400)
  ELSE WHEN prop(this.final, 'is_error') == True: 'claude reported an error: ' + str(prop(this.final, 'result'))
  ELSE: None
ChatMessage.answer getter:
  WHEN this.rr == None: None
  ELSE WHEN this.failed != None: this.failed
  ELSE WHEN this.capped: this.spoken + '\n\n(stopped at the ceiling of ' + str(this.max_turns) + ' turns)'
  ELSE WHEN strip(str(prop(this.final, 'result') or '')) != '': str(prop(this.final, 'result'))
  ELSE: this.spoken
ChatMessage.tools_names getter: words(join([join([replace(str(prop(b, 'name')), 'mcp__membrane__', '') for b in (prop(prop(e, 'message'), 'content') or []) if prop(b, 'type') == 'tool_use'], ' ') for e in this.evs if prop(e, 'type') == 'assistant'], ' '))
Chat.answer on-setter turn-finish:
  WHEN this.answer != None:
    this.state = 'error' if this.failed != None else 'done'
    this.tools_run = this.tools_names
    membrane::Chat:message[this.mid]:response = ChatResponse(text: this.answer, error: this.failed != None, rc: this.rc)
    FOR e IN [x for x in this.evs if prop(x, 'type') == 'assistant']:
      FOR b IN [y for y in (prop(prop(e, 'message'), 'content') or []) if prop(y, 'type') == 'tool_use']:
        membrane::Chat:message[this.mid]:tool[prop(b, 'id')] = ChatTool(name: prop(b, 'name'), input: prop(b, 'input'))
    FOR e IN [x for x in this.evs if prop(x, 'type') == 'user']:
      FOR b IN [y for y in (prop(prop(e, 'message'), 'content') or []) if prop(y, 'type') == 'tool_result']:
        body = prop(b, 'content')
        membrane::Chat:message[this.mid]:tool[prop(b, 'tool_use_id')].result = Text(body) or join([prop(c, 'text') for c in (List(body) or [])], '\n')
